From: Alex Scotti <alexscotti@gmail.com>
Subject: amdv: an EL taken for a BL it does not belong to is handed back

Found in review, traced in the code: with FLAG_CHECK_ES_PTS set, a BL
whose dvel_vf_get() returned an EL with another pts logged "not found el"
and moved on - the EL was neither paired nor put, so each mismatch held
one EL decoder buffer until the decoder ran out and stalled. The flag is
off by default; it is the one to set to chase a pairing skew (9012), and
then it must not wedge the decoder. Both parse paths now put the EL back.
---
 drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
index 7f0d1ba..1c651a4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/enhancement/amdolby_vision/amdv.c
@@ -8749,6 +8749,11 @@ int amdv_parse_metadata_v1(struct vframe_s *vf,
 					("bl(%p-%lld) not found el(%p-%lld)\n",
 					 vf, vf->pts_us64,
 					 el_vf, el_vf->pts_us64);
+				/* not this BL's EL: hand it back, or the EL
+				 * decoder runs out of buffers
+				 */
+				if (el_vf)
+					dvel_vf_put(el_vf);
 			}
 		} else if (toggle_mode == 1) {
 			if (debug_dolby & 2)
@@ -10419,6 +10424,12 @@ int amdv_parse_metadata_v2_stb(struct vframe_s *vf,
 					("bl(%p-%lld) not found el(%p-%lld)\n",
 					 vf, vf->pts_us64,
 					 el_vf, el_vf->pts_us64);
+				/* An EL taken but not this BL's (FLAG_CHECK_ES_PTS):
+				 * it was never handed back, and the EL decoder
+				 * stalled once it ran out of buffers.
+				 */
+				if (el_vf)
+					dvel_vf_put(el_vf);
 				/* Its EL is owed from now on: dvel_retire_owed()
 				 * counts this BL until it is put.
 				 */
